Relevant columns for the question  
• `event_date`: filter to 20210102.  
• `event_name`: keep only 'page_view'.  
• `event_params`:  - `key = 'page_location'`  ➜ full URL of the page that was viewed.  
                   - `key = 'ga_session_id'`  ➜ session identifier (together with `user_pseudo_id`).  
• `user_pseudo_id`: user identifier used to group sessions.  
• `event_timestamp`: allows us to order hits inside the same session so we can decide which page was viewed first.  

Typical conditions that will be used  
```
WHERE event_date = '20210102'
  AND event_name = 'page_view'
```  
PLP pattern (case–insensitive, NO “+” in 4‑th or 5‑th segment, but one of the category names must be present):  
```
REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(url_seg4), r'(accessories|apparel|brands|campus collection|drinkware|electronics|google redesign|lifestyle|nest|new 2015 logo|notebooks journals|office|shop by brand|small goods|stationery|wearables)')
AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(url_seg4, r'\+')
```
(or the same for `url_seg5`)  

PDP pattern (same categories, last segment *does* contain “+”):  
```
REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(url_last), r'\+')
AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(url_seg4|url_seg5), r'(accessories|apparel …)')
```


